"o200k_base proxy tokens) in application/aggregation. I read all six "
"bounded pages. Static inspection only: I did not run aggregations, access"
" encrypted repositories, perform a filing, or verify legal references "
"against current law. The code uses bundled and generation-pinned data, "
"which this review treats as implementation inputs rather than verified "
"law."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:14
msgid "Operator previews and evidence policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:16
msgid ""
"The M347/M349 counterpart aggregator is an operator-supplied preview "
"surface, not the live calculation source mesh. It reads dated operation-"
"kind and readiness declarations through a pinned registry operation, "
"validates the selected model revision and registry token vocabulary, "
"groups by source kind, counterparty NIF and operation kind, rejects "
"conflicting countries within a cohort, and reports totals and readiness. "
"M349 readiness is conditional on country: the configured GROI country "
"requires GROI verification; non-GROI countries may require NIF-IVA "
"verification. M347 returns unthresholded totals because the declaration "
"floor is enforced in the binding consumer. The strict frozen input "
"requires the country rather than assuming Spain, and typed "
"country/date/period fields constrain the operator payload. Counterpart "
"payload and aggregation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/counterpart.py`) Model entry points"
" and threshold boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/counterpart.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:18
msgid ""
"Currency helpers distinguish raw EUR from converted foreign currency. "
"General ledger projections can use a preconverted amount and apply the "
"same FX rate to native taxable base and IVA; an unconverted foreign row "
"raises a typed configuration error rather than contaminating EUR totals. "
"The transaction IVA admission path in the prior chunk has a stricter tax-"
"substrate rule, so this helper’s availability should not be read as "
"universal permission to convert every kind of tax fact. EUR amount and "
"taxable-base helpers "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/currency_predicates.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:20
msgid ""
"The IVA evidence advisory fires only for active business-bearing rows "
"with positive quota in a quota-bearing category. It applies a stronger "
"test to deductible input IVA (purchase-invoice evidence or a validated "
"catalogue invoice) than to output IVA (any linked evidence), with the "
"former marked blocking at verification and the latter visible but non-"
"blocking. Evidence trigger and output evidence test "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/evidence_advisory.py`) Diagnostic "
"construction (`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/evidence_advisory.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:22
msgid ""
"A narrow boundary question remains: the output-side helper counts "
"purchase-invoice-evidence ID or attachment IDs, but not "
"Transaction.invoice_id, even though the module describes any linked "
"document as enough and its deductible-side helper explicitly counts "
"invoice_id. If a valid issued invoice linked by invoice_id is an accepted"
" output document in this flow, the current advisory can still report "
"missing evidence. This is a non-blocking false-warning risk, conditional "
"on that invoice-link shape being reachable; trace the output evidence "
"contract before calling it a defect. Output evidence membership "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/evidence_advisory.py`) Deductible "
"evidence membership "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/evidence_advisory.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:24
msgid "Foreign assets and inventory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:26
msgid ""
"Modelo 720 foreign-asset observations accept four canonical source kinds,"
" constrain currencies to a nonnegative EUR valuation, validate countries "
"and real ISO date strings, and require ledger transaction IDs to meet the"
" canonical identity format. Aggregation produces per-source/per-class "
"rollups; a separate threshold step sums classes within each registry "
"obligation block and marks all present classes declarable when the block "
"exceeds its initial floor. This separation exposes raw totals and leaves "
"filing applicability to the selected, dated threshold data. 720 "
"observation boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/foreign_assets.py`) Obligation-"
"block thresholds "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/foreign_assets.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:28
msgid ""
"The repository-free source resolver accepts typed observations or "
"already-validated worksheet rows. For observations, it filters to "
"threshold-selected classes and binds row values to the selected M720 "
"revision, but intentionally emits no provenance because there is no "
"authoritative persisted asset identity; ledger transaction IDs are "
"carried separately. The worksheet path can instead build row identities "
"and content fingerprints from validated detail records. Thus a valid "
"aggregate preview does not by itself establish a grounded calculation "
"source. Resolver and aggregate path "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/foreign_assets.py`) No-provenance "
"aggregate result "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/foreign_assets.py`) Worksheet row "
"identities (`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/foreign_assets.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:30
msgid ""
"The inventory resolver reads one injected encrypted ledger repository. "
"Before storage access it checks the binding cohort uses the exact "
"canonical row operations and selected filing coordinate, and checks year "
"applicability. A profile that explicitly declares no economic activity "
"makes the source inapplicable; otherwise absent repository, unreadable "
"storage, missing activity ledgers, invalid row templates, or projection "
"inconsistency return unresolved bindings with typed diagnostics. A valid "
"projection generates the three values for each activity, a fingerprint, "
"primary provenance, and a non-blocking physical-closing-conflict "
"diagnostic where applicable. The resolver does not invent a manual "
"fallback or aggregate across activities. Template, storage and projection"
" flow (`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/inventory.py`) Inventory row "
"projection and provenance "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/inventory.py`) Source resolver "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/inventory.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:32
msgid ""
"One privacy detail merits downstream tracing. Inventory provenance uses a"
" content digest rather than actividad_id and says the taxpayer’s activity"
" identifier is not disclosable, but RowSourceIdentity separately stores "
"projection.actividad_id as source_row_identity. This module does not "
"establish whether that identity is persisted or exposed in explanations; "
"verify the downstream serialization and redaction before concluding it is"
" private. Content-addressed provenance "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/inventory.py`) Plain source-row "
"identity (`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/inventory.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:34
msgid "Income ledgers and invoice timing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:36
msgid ""
"The impatriado ledger loads only from a caller-supplied repository bound "
"to the requested bucket and date-partitions annual reads. Active incoming"
" rows are admitted against the revision-selected source-jurisdiction and "
"income-category sets; unresolved/out-of-scope jurisdiction, unsupported "
"currency, absent business attribution, and out-of-window rows become "
"typed issues. Governed eligible categories admit the full value; other "
"income uses business proportion. Gross and optional taxable base are "
"converted to EUR consistently and scaled by the same proportion, then "
"folded to the selected target casilla. Repository partition and bucket "
"check (`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/impatriado_income_ledger.py`)"
" Transaction classification and EUR projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/impatriado_income_ledger.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:38
msgid ""
"The M210 IRNR ledger similarly checks the injected revision against "
"authority selection, reads income-code namespace and source-jurisdiction "
"scope from that revision, validates the selected official code, and "
"optionally date-partitions the repository. Active incoming rows outside "
"the target scope or missing a declared classification yield traceable "
"issues; only rows matching the selected two-character income code reach "
"the output. The classification’s explicit gross income, applicable rate, "
"payer mode, and optional payer/asset IDs are carried forward rather than "
"reconstructed from signed cash. This makes operator-entered "
"classification a critical input contract. IRNR repository flow "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/irnr_income_ledger.py`) Selected "
"revision and projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/irnr_income_ledger.py`) Registry "
"code namespace "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/irnr_income_ledger.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:40
msgid ""
"Invoice devengo is represented as both a date and a rank: declared "
"operation/advance date or issue-date proxy. One shared predicate uses "
"that result for period membership, and a non-blocking diagnostic names "
"proxy-attributed invoices so the operator can record operation dates. A "
"staged series of partial advance payments is explicitly unrepresentable "
"in this one-date model. The direction-only bank mapping has another "
"explicit limitation: an incoming refund of a purchase maps to "
"ISSUED/output IVA, because the two-member invoice-kind axis cannot "
"express a signed correction; consolidating that decision avoids "
"duplicated drift but does not solve the refund treatment. Devengo "
"resolution and period membership "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/invoice_devengo.py`) Proxy advisory"
" (`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/invoice_devengo.py`) Direction "
"mapping and refund limit "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/invoice_kind.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:42
msgid ""
"Received-invoice withholding is a projection into the existing per-"
"perceptor store, not another persistence path. The application reads "
"liability/base and identity from a received invoice, requires declared "
"scheme and recipient/payment or exigibility evidence from the request, "
"rejects nonresident suppliers from this IRPF path, and submits one "
"capture command to a shared producer with idempotency, mode, baseline, "
"supersession, and annual-detail evidence. The projection accumulates all "
"defects and either yields a typed observation or a defect-only refusal; "
"it does not infer scheme from invoice kind. The request’s allocation "
"values are caller supplied, while the invoice supplies the source "
"liability snapshot; the downstream producer owns write/consistency "
"enforcement. Invoice withholding capture builder "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/invoice_retencion.py`) Projection "
"and liability defects "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/invoice_retencion.py`) Defect sweep"
" (`src/cadrumo/application/aggregation/invoice_retencion.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:44
msgid "Assessment and dependencies"
msgstr "Evaluación y dependencias"

#: ../../technical/articles/032-aggregation-sources-evidence-and-withholding-projections.md:46
msgid ""
"Strong patterns include registry-selected applicability, explicit EUR "
"conversion helpers, date-partitioned repository reads, strict source IDs,"
" typed exclusions, and a visible distinction between blocking deductible "
"evidence and advisory-only output evidence. Important limits are equally "
"explicit: 347/349 is a preview, aggregate M720 observations lack primary "
"provenance, partial advance schedules are unsupported, refunds are not "
"modeled by invoice kind, and IRNR gross/rate classifications depend on "
"input facts. No tests are included in these modules; runtime "
"reachability, repository encryption, operator display of diagnostics, and"
" final persistence behavior remain unverified. Follow up on the output "
"evidence membership question and inventory activity-ID exposure through "
"downstream persistence. Dependencies include the shared grouping helpers,"
" transaction/invoice repository protocols, selected modelo and obligation"
" registries, the sealed inventory projection, invoice catalogue, and "
"shared withholding producer. Do not treat descriptions of tax law in "
"docstrings as current legal verification."
msgstr ""

